{"name":"Pink Glamour","hex":"#ff1dcd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"glamour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Originally, enchantment; magic charm; especially, the effect of a spell that causes one to see objects in a form that differs from reality, typically to make filthy, ugly, or repulsive things seem beauteous.","Alluring beauty or charm (often with sex appeal)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enchant; to bewitch.","↑ Postrel, Virginia (5 November 2013), “One: The Magic of Glamour”, in The Power of Glamour: Longing and the Art of Visual Persuasion, Simon & Schuster, →ISBN: “Reflecting this sense of the word, by 1902 Webster's included two new definitions: “a kind of haze in the air, causing things to appear different from what they really are”…”"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glamour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glamour","blocks":[{"text":"In the field of cultural studies, glamour is the impression of attraction or fascination that a particularly luxurious or elegant appearance creates, an impression which intensifies reality. Usually, a person, event, location, technology, or product such as a piece of clothing can be glamorous or add glamour. \"Glamour\" originally referred to a magic spell, an illusion said to be cast by witches."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lana_Turner_by_Paul_Hesse_1946.jpg/330px-Lana_Turner_by_Paul_Hesse_1946.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glamour","wikidata":"Q390104"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Chrysler_building-_top.jpg/500px-Chrysler_building-_top.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Chrysler_building-_top.jpg/500px-Chrysler_building-_top.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Art deco, as seen here on the Chrysler Building  in Midtown Manhattan, is often characterised as glamorous.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChrysler_building-_top.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Aston.db5.coupe.300pix.jpg/250px-Aston.db5.coupe.300pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d3/Aston.db5.coupe.300pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Aston.db5.coupe.300pix.jpg/250px-Aston.db5.coupe.300pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Aston Martin DB5 as seen in Goldfinger. Expensive items are often part of a glamorous lifestyle.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAston.db5.coupe.300pix.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Norma_Shearer%2C_Rosalind_Russell_and_Joan_Crawford_in_The_Women.jpg/500px-Norma_She